		{"id":"c411f0f96be183a3","type":"group","x":-3310,"y":-1280,"width":900,"height":675,"label":"After"},
		{"id":"ace7c4bfbdf2a8e9","type":"group","x":-4320,"y":-1265,"width":820,"height":720,"label":"Before"},
		{"id":"ba441ee581676186","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (Before)\n\nVena Solutions is a cloud-native FP&A platform that integrates seamlessly with Microsoft 365, enabling collaborative budgeting, forecasting, and reporting for over 2,000 clients across various industries. The platform utilizes a multi-dimensional model encompassing Accounts, Departments, Entities, Periods, and Scenarios, ensuring dimensional integrity and scenario validation. Its data ecosystem includes a General Ledger (GL) source, which provides critical financial data through account_master, departments_data, and journal_entries tables, supporting comprehensive financial reporting. Vena maintains a robust validation framework with 20+ quality checks focused on completeness and consistency, enhancing operational accuracy and decision-making.","x":-8702,"y":785,"width":560,"height":360},
		{"id":"22739da2e8dcdc4d","type":"text","text":"**rule_id: 123**\n**rule_name: xyz**\n\n\n* get all the rule names and business rules for given source_id\n* LLM call includes context of rules, names and inferred source description and embedding input.\n* reinfer the source metadata\n* again reinfer the client metadata with context of reinferred source and inferred client context.","x":-348,"y":-201,"width":788,"height":481},
		{"id":"92e30a3113bf23c9","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (After)\nVena Solutions operates a cloud-native FP&A platform that integrates with Microsoft 365, facilitating collaborative budgeting, forecasting, and reporting for over 2,000 clients. The platform utilizes a multi-dimensional model encompassing Accounts, Departments, Entities, Periods, and Scenarios, ensuring dimensional integrity and scenario validation. The data ecosystem includes 1 source, the General Ledger (GL), which supports accurate financial reporting and analysis through 55 validation rules focused on referential integrity, completeness, and consistency. This comprehensive validation framework enhances data quality across source-level, table-level, and column-level checks, ensuring reliable financial insights and decision-making.","x":-8102,"y":785,"width":500,"height":360},
		{"id":"8c8669da7456b2a5","type":"text","text":"### Description (Before)\nVena Solutions operates in the Financial Technology sector, providing an AI-powered financial planning and analysis platform that enhances budgeting, forecasting, and reporting for businesses, particularly those utilizing Microsoft Excel.","x":-8702,"y":525,"width":540,"height":220},
		{"id":"e93b4e33e5305e98","type":"text","text":"### Description (After)\n\nVena Solutions is a leading AI-powered financial planning and analysis (FP&A) platform in the FinTech industry, focusing on enhancing budgeting, forecasting, and reporting processes through seamless integrations with Microsoft 365.","x":-8102,"y":525,"width":480,"height":220},
		{"id":"bc0967361e3f0f28","type":"text","text":"The ERP source serves as a critical component in Vena's financial planning and analysis ecosystem, enabling finance teams to manage and analyze financial data with high accuracy and integrity. This source encompasses three key tables: Dimensions, Transactions, and Fiscal_Calendar, which collectively support the organization's goal of ensuring data quality for financial reporting and compliance. The Dimensions table likely contains various attributes related to financial entities, while the Transactions table captures detailed financial activities, and the Fiscal_Calendar table provides essential temporal context for financial data. By integrating these tables, Vena facilitates comprehensive data validation and reporting processes, allowing finance teams to transition from reactive to proactive decision-making. The ERP source plays a vital role in reducing month-end close times and enhancing budgeting cycles, ultimately driving more accurate forecasting and strategic financial management across diverse industries such as banking, healthcare, manufacturing, and SaaS. This source's architecture supports seamless data integration patterns, ensuring that all financial transactions and planning processes are underpinned by reliable, validated data.","x":-4300,"y":-885,"width":780,"height":320},
		{"id":"5c6f60e094cf4cbd","type":"text","text":"The ERP source serves as a critical component of the Canadian Opera Company's financial data ecosystem, encompassing three key tables: Dimensions, which contains various attributes related to financial entities; Transactions, which records detailed financial transactions for analysis and reporting; and Fiscal_Calendar, which holds fiscal year and period information essential for financial reporting. This source supports the organization's operational workflows by ensuring accurate financial tracking and compliance with Canadian arts regulations. It facilitates decision-making processes by providing a structured approach to financial data management, enabling stakeholders to analyze performance, manage budgets, and ensure fiscal accountability. The integration of these tables allows for comprehensive reporting and analysis, aligning with the COC's strategic focus on inclusivity and sustainability in the performing arts.","x":-3270,"y":-885,"width":840,"height":260},
		{"id":"18a51ce5db7db5be","type":"text","text":"The ERP source provides essential financial data through its Dimensions, Transactions, and Fiscal_Calendar tables, supporting the Canadian Opera Company's operational and reporting needs.","x":-3290,"y":-1260,"width":440,"height":122},
		{"id":"fc45b3b3fffb4696","type":"text","text":"The ERP source provides essential financial data management capabilities, supporting accurate financial planning and analysis across various industries.\n\n\n","x":-4270,"y":-1245,"width":481,"height":107},
		{"id":"e38262dc0d6405a7","type":"text","text":"## client_dq_rule\nVena Solutions enforces 55 data quality rules (41 business rules, 14 technical rules) as part of its robust data quality governance framework, which is essential for maintaining the integrity and reliability of its AI-powered financial planning and analysis platform. This framework ensures that all financial data utilized in budgeting, forecasting, and reporting processes adheres to strict validation standards, thereby enhancing operational excellence for businesses leveraging Microsoft Excel. The governance policies mandate that all department references in the General Ledger must be valid, ensuring cross-source data consistency and accountability through rules that require non-null manager names for departments and valid email formats. Furthermore, the framework emphasizes the importance of unique transaction identifiers and properly formatted journal entries, which are critical for accurate financial reporting and decision-making. The distinction between business rules, such as ensuring that budget allocations are supported by valid headcounts, and technical rules, which enforce data type integrity and format compliance, is crucial for maintaining data quality across the organization. Vena Solutions' commitment to data quality includes regulatory compliance measures, ensuring that all financial transactions are recorded within the correct accounting periods and that all entries reference valid accounts, thus preserving the trustworthiness of financial data. The client-level quality standards also encompass comprehensive validation patterns, quality thresholds, and acceptance criteria that are vital for ensuring data fitness for strategic decision-making. By implementing these rigorous data quality rules, Vena Solutions not only protects the integrity of its financial data but also enhances the overall reliability and accuracy of its financial reporting processes, ultimately supporting its clients' operational and financial goals.","x":-6971,"y":3000,"width":900,"height":500},
		{"id":"34445f019a71b614","type":"text","text":"## table_dq_rule\nThe account_master table implements 17 data quality rules (9 business rules, 8 technical rules) ensuring robust data quality validation for financial accounts critical to effective financial management and reporting. The validation framework mandates that the Account_Code must be unique for each Account_Type, preventing confusion and ensuring distinct identification of account types. Technical rules enforce that Account_ID, Account_Code, Account_Name, Account_Type, Description, Parent_Account, Currency_Code, and Created_By fields must not be NULL, guaranteeing that every account is identifiable, categorized, and has a descriptive context, which is essential for financial management. Business rules stipulate that if an account's Status is 'Active', then a valid Created_Timestamp must be present, ensuring accurate tracking of account history. The Status field must be either 'Active' or 'Inactive', validating the account's state for accurate financial reporting. Furthermore, the Modified_Timestamp must exceed the last modification time for Modified_By, ensuring integrity in change tracking. The Reporting_Category, Cost_Center_Default, Notes, and Is_Tax_Relevant fields must not be NULL, ensuring comprehensive context for financial reporting and compliance. The Is_Tax_Relevant field must only contain 'Yes' or 'No', ensuring valid tax applicability for accurate calculations. These quality checks protect data integrity and support operational reliability, ensuring that the account_master table serves as a trustworthy repository for financial data, facilitating budgeting, forecasting, and strategic financial planning.","x":-6971,"y":4180,"width":900,"height":440},
		{"id":"fd5d34e449d13ee3","type":"text","text":"## source_dq_rule \nThe General Ledger (GL) source implements 55 data quality rules (41 business rules, 14 technical rules) that establish a robust framework for financial data integrity and accountability. This source prioritizes validation standards that ensure all department references in account_master are valid, with business rules mandating that the Department_ID in GL.account_master must match existing entries in GL.departments_data, thereby preserving referential integrity. Additionally, the GL source enforces critical quality checks such as ensuring that every department with a name has an associated manager, and that all email addresses conform to valid formats, which are essential for maintaining communication accuracy and organizational accountability. The GL journal entries are subjected to rigorous validation, requiring unique transaction IDs and valid account references to ensure that financial transactions are accurately tracked and reported. The source also emphasizes data completeness and accuracy, with rules ensuring that all journal entries have valid timestamps and that amounts are greater than zero, thus preventing erroneous financial reporting. Furthermore, the GL source maintains consistency across its data by enforcing that all entries utilize a uniform currency code of 'USD', which is vital for coherent financial analysis. Technical rules complement these business validations by ensuring that all account identifiers are non-null and correctly formatted, thereby enhancing the reliability of financial data. The GL source's governance framework mandates that all modifications are timestamped and attributed to responsible individuals, ensuring accountability and a clear audit trail. Overall, the General Ledger serves as a foundational source for financial management, with its comprehensive data quality rules ensuring that financial accounts, departmental details, and transaction records are accurate, complete, and reliable, ultimately supporting effective financial decision-making and compliance.","x":-6971,"y":3600,"width":900,"height":500},
		{"id":"2a06e43142531862","type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<timestamp>\",\n  \"name\": \"<source_name>\",\n  \"lookup_id\": \"<source_id>\",\n  \"type\": \"source_dq\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"<Summary of source and dq_rules>\",\n  \"embedding_vector\": []\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<timestamp>\",\n  \"name\": \"<table_name>\",\n  \"lookup_id\": \"<table_id>\",\n  \"type\": \"table_dq\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"<Summary of table and dq_rules>\",\n  \"embedding_vector\": []\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<timestamp>\",\n  \"name\": \"<client_name>\",\n  \"lookup_id\": \"<client_id>\",\n  \"type\": \"client_dq\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"<Summary of client and dq_rules>\",\n  \"embedding_vector\": []\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<timestamp>\",\n  \"lookup_id\": \"<client_name>\",\n  \"name\": \"<client_id>\",\n  \"type\": \"client_metadata\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"\",\n  \"collection_name\": \"client_metadata\",\n  \"embedding_vector\":[]\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<timestamp>\",\n  \"lookup_id\": \"<source_id>\",\n  \"name\": \"<source_name>\",\n  \"type\": \"source_metadata\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"\",\n  \"collection_name\": \"source_metadata\",\n  \"embedding_vector\":[]\n}\n```\n\n```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"<timestamp>\",\n  \"lookup_id\": \"<table_id>\",\n  \"name\": \"<table_name>\",\n  \"type\": \"table_metadata\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"\",\n  \"collection_name\": \"table_metadata\",\n  \"embedding_vector\":[]\n}\n```","x":-5520,"y":3000,"width":1060,"height":1480},
		{"id":"b83c9463bad15809","type":"text","text":"### Description (Before)\nThe General Ledger (GL) source provides essential financial data through its account_master, departments_data, and journal_entries tables, supporting comprehensive financial reporting and analysis.","x":-8702,"y":1463,"width":560,"height":200},
		{"id":"3e99bcc5e393b06c","type":"text","text":"### Description (After)\n\nThe General Ledger (GL) source provides essential financial data through its tables, including account details, departmental information, and journal entries, supporting accurate financial reporting and analysis.","x":-8062,"y":1463,"width":460,"height":200},
		{"id":"57c9bbfc50c0e0fd","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (Before)\n\nThe General Ledger (GL) serves as a critical source within Vena Solutions' FP&A platform, facilitating the management of financial data across multiple dimensions such as Accounts, Departments, and Scenarios. It encompasses three key tables: account_master, which details financial accounts including identifiers and classifications; departments_data, which provides insights into departmental structures and budget allocations; and journal_entries, which records all financial transactions through detailed journal entries. This source supports operational decision-making and analytical workflows by ensuring dimensional integrity and scenario validation, thereby enhancing the accuracy of Actuals, Budgets, and Forecasts. The GL implements 20+ validation rules focusing on referential integrity and business logic, maintaining comprehensive validation coverage across table and column levels to ensure data quality and governance maturity.","x":-8702,"y":1743,"width":560,"height":520},
		{"id":"30da08263f8d6962","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (After)\nThe General Ledger (GL) source serves as a critical component of the financial planning and analysis ecosystem, integrating data from three key tables: account_master, departments_data, and journal_entries. The account_master table maintains comprehensive details about financial accounts, including identifiers, classifications, and statuses, ensuring dimensional integrity and facilitating accurate reporting. The departments_data table captures detailed information about organizational departments, encompassing identifiers, management details, and budget allocations, which are vital for departmental financial oversight. The journal_entries table records detailed transactions, providing a historical account of financial activities. This source implements 55+ validation rules across various scopes, including source-level checks for referential integrity and table-level validations for data consistency, ensuring high data quality and governance maturity. Key validation focus areas include account referencing, department integrity, and transaction accuracy, supporting robust decision-making workflows and analytical requirements within the organization.","x":-8062,"y":1743,"width":460,"height":520},
		{"id":"0f184e4ccd4d56fc","type":"text","text":"### Description (Before)\nVena Solutions operates in the Financial Technology (FinTech) sector, providing an AI-powered financial planning and analysis platform that enhances budgeting, forecasting, and reporting for businesses.","x":-10360,"y":525,"width":540,"height":220},
		{"id":"1c8197630e371346","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (Before)\n\nVena Solutions is a cloud-native FP&A platform that integrates seamlessly with Microsoft 365, focusing on collaborative budgeting, forecasting, and reporting. It utilizes a multi-dimensional model to support driver-based planning and scenario analysis, managing Actuals, Budgets, and Forecasts from ERP, CRM, and HR data. The platform's key data source, the General Ledger (GL), underpins financial reporting and analysis by maintaining detailed records of accounts and departmental allocations. Vena's AI-driven insights, powered by Vena Copilot, enhance decision-making for over 2,000 clients across various industries, including SaaS and healthcare, emphasizing the importance of Excel in financial planning.","x":-10360,"y":785,"width":560,"height":360},
		{"id":"690bfb58df6a4d1b","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (After)\nVena Solutions, a leader in Financial Technology, offers a cloud-native FP&A platform integrated with Microsoft 365, facilitating collaborative budgeting, forecasting, and reporting. The platform utilizes a multi-dimensional model to manage Actuals, Budgets, and Forecasts, ensuring data accuracy through 59 validation rules applied to its General Ledger (GL) source. These rules, including Department ID Consistency and Email Format Validation, enhance data integrity and support operational efficiency. Vena's AI-driven insights and automation tools empower over 2,000 customers across various industries, emphasizing the importance of Excel in financial planning.","x":-9760,"y":785,"width":500,"height":360},
		{"id":"2ed8788cbdb334ab","type":"text","text":"### Description (After)\n\nVena Solutions operates in the Financial Technology (FinTech) sector, providing an AI-powered financial planning and analysis platform that enhances budgeting, forecasting, and reporting for businesses using Microsoft 365.","x":-9760,"y":525,"width":480,"height":220},
		{"id":"862d6e13a0ecab96","type":"text","text":"### Description (Before)\nThe General Ledger (GL) serves as a foundational source for financial reporting and analysis, encompassing detailed records of accounts, departmental allocations, and journal entries.","x":-10360,"y":1505,"width":560,"height":200},
		{"id":"3bfc359b5357a6d5","type":"text","text":"### Description (After)\n\nThe General Ledger (GL) serves as a foundational source for financial reporting and analysis, encompassing detailed records of accounts, departmental allocations, and journal entries.","x":-9720,"y":1505,"width":460,"height":200},
		{"id":"4a108545a2300e83","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (Before)\n\nThe General Ledger (GL) is a critical component of Vena Solutions' FP&A platform, providing a comprehensive view of financial data essential for budgeting, forecasting, and reporting. It integrates with various data sources, including ERP, CRM, and HR systems, to manage Actuals, Budgets, and Forecasts. The GL consists of three key tables: account_master, which details financial accounts for tracking and reporting; departments_data, which outlines departmental financial allocations and management; and journal_entries, which records all financial transactions. This multi-dimensional model supports driver-based planning and variance analysis, ensuring dimensional integrity and scenario validation. The GL plays a vital role in operational support and decision-making workflows, enabling organizations to derive insights and maintain accuracy in financial reporting.","x":-10360,"y":1785,"width":560,"height":520},
		{"id":"cb83cdf00d902254","type":"text","text":"### Embedding input (After)\nThe General Ledger (GL) is a critical component of Vena Solutions' FP&A platform, providing a comprehensive view of financial data essential for budgeting, forecasting, and reporting. It integrates with various data sources, including ERP, CRM, and HR systems, to manage Actuals, Budgets, and Forecasts. The GL consists of three key tables: account_master, which details financial accounts for tracking and reporting; departments_data, which outlines departmental financial allocations and management; and journal_entries, which records all financial transactions. This multi-dimensional model supports driver-based planning and variance analysis, ensuring dimensional integrity and scenario validation. The GL plays a vital role in operational support and decision-making workflows, enabling organizations to derive insights and maintain accuracy in financial reporting.","x":-9720,"y":1785,"width":460,"height":520},
